 "summary": "Mostly no: nearly every drawdown setting did the same as random entries on BTC, ETH and SOL. One result holds up. On 1h, long entries while price was more than 20% under its 100-bar high beat random by 1.52% after 20 candles, and the result held without its strongest stretch. The same setting on 4h and daily was the same as random.",
 "verdicts": [
  {
   "use": "Buying a deep drop (more than 20% under the 100-bar high)",
   "verdict": "edge",
   "text": "Beat random on 1h by 1.52% after 20 candles. It also beat random at 10 and 50 candles, and it held without its strongest stretch. On 4h and daily it was the same as random."
  },
  {
   "use": "Buying a 10% dip (more than 10%, or 10% to 20%, under the high)",
   "verdict": "none",
   "text": "Same as random on 1h and 4h. On daily, more than 10% under had too few separate moves to judge."
  },
  {
   "use": "Buying the cross down through 10%",
   "verdict": "none",
   "text": "Same as random on 1h, 4h and daily. Buying on the candle the drawdown first passed 10% added nothing."
  },
  {
   "use": "Shorting near the high (within 5%)",
   "verdict": "none",
   "text": "Same as random on 1h, 4h and daily. Price near its 100-bar high did not tend to reverse."
  }
 ],
 "notes": [
  "On 1h, buying while price was more than 20% under its 100-bar high gave 4,022 entries in 183 separate moves. Twenty candles later these entries were 1.52% ahead of random entries, above a luck band of -0.49% to 0.61%. The result held without its strongest stretch, 54 entries on Sep 16–18, 2020. It also showed at 10 and 50 candles but was gone by 100.",
  "This 1h result comes from uptrends. While the pair closed above its 200-day SMA, the same entries beat random by 2.4%. In downtrends they were 0.51% ahead, which is inside the luck band, so they did the same as random. A deep pullback inside an uptrend recovered. A deep drop in a falling market did not.",
  "By coin, ETH beat random by 0.98% and SOL by 1.53%. BTC had only 21 separate moves, under the 30 needed for a verdict, so it was never judged. On 4h the same setting was 0.02% behind random. On daily it was 0.6% behind. Both are inside the band.",
  "Shallower drawdowns showed nothing. On 1h, more than 10% under the high fires about seven times as often as the 20% setting, and it ended 0.16% ahead of random, inside the band. The 10% to 20% zone was 0.07% behind. The cross down through 10% did the same as random on every timeframe. In 1h downtrends that cross beat random by 0.34%, but only because of 3 entries on Feb 27–28, 2022. Without those entries it was the same as random, and it showed nothing at 10, 50 or 100 candles.",
  "Shorting within 5% of the 100-bar high on 1h gave 88,051 entries and ended 0.06% ahead of random, inside a band of -0.06% to 0.09%. On 4h and daily it was also the same as random. On daily, every setting had too few downtrend moves to judge, so the daily numbers say nothing about falling markets.",
  "For a long bot on 1h, more than 20% under the 100-bar high works best as a filter beside a trend condition, such as the pair being above its 200-day SMA. The move after it showed within 10 to 50 candles and was gone by 100, so size the take profit for that window. In downtrends the setting showed nothing, and that is where it fails. The 10% levels and the near-high short did the same as random, so leave them out and let the DCA orders and take profit do the work."
 ],
